# pocket-home for Debian

To build a deb file for `pocket-home` targeting `armhf` on Debian Jessie, follow these instructions:

Since Debian Jessie is EOL, `debootstrap` needs to point to the archive repo, and `apt` configurations need to bypass the `Valid-Until` check.
Here is the step-by-step process using `qemu-user-static` and `debootstrap` to natively compile the deb file on an Ubuntu/Debian host using a chroot.

```bash
# 1. Install prerequisites for creating an armhf chroot
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install -y qemu-user-static binfmt-support debootstrap schroot

# 2. Bootstrap the Debian Jessie armhf environment
sudo debootstrap --arch=armhf jessie jessie-chroot http://archive.debian.org/debian/

# 3. Create a setup script to configure the chroot environment
cat << 'CHROOT_EOF' > setup_chroot.sh
#!/bin/bash
dpkg --configure -a
echo 'deb http://archive.debian.org/debian/ jessie main contrib non-free' > /etc/apt/sources.list
echo 'Acquire::Check-Valid-Until false;' > /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99no-check-valid-until
apt-get update --allow-unauthenticated
apt-get install -y --force-yes build-essential debhelper libx11-dev libxext-dev libxinerama-dev libxrandr-dev libxcursor-dev libfreetype6-dev libasound2-dev libi2c-dev pkg-config
CHROOT_EOF

# 4. Copy the setup script and run it inside the chroot
sudo cp setup_chroot.sh jessie-chroot/
sudo chroot jessie-chroot /bin/bash /setup_chroot.sh

# 5. Copy the source code to the chroot
sudo mkdir -p jessie-chroot/src
sudo rsync -a --exclude 'jessie-chroot' . jessie-chroot/src/

# 6. Create a script to run the build process
cat << 'BUILD_EOF' > build_deb.sh
#!/bin/bash
cd /src
make -j$(nproc)
dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
BUILD_EOF

sudo cp build_deb.sh jessie-chroot/
sudo chroot jessie-chroot /bin/bash /build_deb.sh

# 7. Retrieve the built deb file from the chroot
sudo cp jessie-chroot/pocket-home_0.0.8_armhf.deb .
```
